{"text": "PEEKSKILL\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n\nEnhance and expand opportunities for young artists and professionals to live, work, and play in a city\nthat combines the best of urban and country life.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS:\n\n+ Overlooks a stunning bay in the Hudson River with panoramic views of the Hudson Highlands.\n+ Located an hour from Grand Central by train and features an express stop on Metro-North.\n- Highlighted by the Peekskill Brewery at the waterfront, bars with carefully curated beer lists, farm-to-table\nrestaurants, and two independent coffee shops.\n+ Abounds with recreational and fitness opportunities including hiking, mountain biking, kayaking, Crossfit,\nyoga, pilates, and volleyball.\n\nEXPERIENCE:\n\n+ Presents numerous arts-centric events including a citywide public arts festival organized by the Hudson\nValley Center for Contemporary Art (located on Main Street) and an open studios event featuring over\n100 artists.\n+ Offers an extensive variety of live music. On weekends, you can often see several shows, all in one night,\nwhile also sampling the diverse selection of food and drink offered by Peekskill\u2019s many bars and restaurants.\n+ Features opportunities to delve into an extensive collection of used books and vinyl records at Bruised\nApple Books and discover vintage treasures and rare antiques at The Coop and Early Electrics.\n\nUNIQUE SKILLS:\n\n+ Comparatively affordable rents and home prices and a mix of historic architecture and new construction\nmake Peekskill the perfect place to find your first \u201creal person\u201d apartment or starter home.\n+ Miles of trails, both along the waterfront and amidst the wooded hills high above it.\n- Block parties on restaurant row and a farmers\u2019 market every summer weekend.\n\nASPIRATIONS (where do you see yourself in five years?):\n\n+ Completing the riverfront ropes course at Charles Point Marina and then celebrating with local craft\nbeer and spirits over a few frames of bowling.\n+ Shopping for locally made goods at the Peekskill Central Market.\n+ Enjoying ice cream at Hudson Creamery after running the entire length of Peekskill\u2019s waterfront trail.\n\nRECOGNITIONS:\n\n+12 \u201cBest of Westchester\u201d Awards in 2015, including Gleason\u2019s craft cocktails and PranaMoon Yoga,\nlocated in a converted hat factory.\n+ OpenTable named The Hudson Room one of the 100 hottest restaurants in the country for 2016.\n+ Westchester Municipal Planning Federation award for the new Scenic Hudson Park at Peekskill Landing.\n\nREFERENCES:\n\n+ 20-something city planner who recovers from trail running in nearby Blue Mountain with a small batch\nIPA and a leisurely game of bocce in Birdsall House\u2019s beer garden.\n+ Recent graduate who goes to happy hour at Taco Dive Bar after their return commute from their\naccounting job in Manhattan.\n+ 30-year-old graphic designer who takes swing dance classes at Embark and does live band karaoke\nat 12 Grapes.",
"words": [
